From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] vfs: mockfs's type number is 24 on SBSA, not 'mock'

mockfs (patch 0011) registers vfc_typenum FT_MOCKFS, 0x6D6F636B ('mock'),
and vfs_init sets maxvfstypenum one past the highest built-in type. lsvfs
(adv_cmds) and getvfsbyname() sysctl every number below vfs.generic.
maxtypenum, so on NeoDarwin lsvfs listed devfs, nullfs and hfs and then
spent about 1.8 billion ENOTSUP sysctls looking like a hang (P4-21
checkpoint 1). statfs's f_type, a short, truncated it as well. No shipping
Apple config builds mockfs, so nothing there sees the large number.

Under GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM, mockfs takes 24, the number after bindfs,
and dynamically added file systems (vfs_fsadd: hfs, zfs) start at 25.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/bsd/vfs/vfs_conf.c b/bsd/vfs/vfs_conf.c
--- a/bsd/vfs/vfs_conf.c
+++ b/bsd/vfs/vfs_conf.c
@@ -109,10 +109,24 @@
 	FT_ROUTEFS = 21,
 	FT_NULLFS = 22,
 	FT_BINDFS = 23,
+#if MOCKFS && defined(GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM)
+	/*
+	 * NeoDarwin: the next number, not 'mock'. vfs_init sets maxvfstypenum
+	 * past the highest built-in type, and lsvfs(1) and getvfsbyname(3)
+	 * walk every number below it (1.8 billion sysctls); statfs's f_type is
+	 * a short, which 'mock' doesn't fit.
+	 */
+	FT_MOCKFS = 24
+#else
 	FT_MOCKFS  = 0x6D6F636B
+#endif
 };
 
+#if MOCKFS && defined(GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM)
+int fstypenumstart = FT_MOCKFS + 1;
+#else
 int fstypenumstart = FT_BINDFS + 1;
+#endif
 /*
  * Set up the filesystem operations for vnodes.
  */
